{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a catalytic intramolecular aminoarylation of unactivated alkenes using aryl sulfonamides. The reaction proceeds via a photoredox-mediated generation of N-centered radicals, followed by a 5-exo-trig cyclization and a desulfonylative 1,4-aryl migration (Smiles-Truce rearrangement) to produce substituted arylethylamines (lactams). Key findings include the use of ortho-substituents to suppress dearomatization and the identification of Ir-1 as an effective photocatalyst.",
